WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.442
A green test suite is not enough to

2
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:02.738
claim that a model works.

3
00:00:03.163 --> 00:00:05.447
This study evaluates a QA instrument, not a

4
00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:06.028
new theory.

5
00:00:06.531 --> 00:00:10.023
Before testing, we fix the domain, units, tolerance,

6
00:00:10.149 --> 00:00:12.490
invariants, and an independent oracle.

7
00:00:12.993 --> 00:00:15.035
Then we run a baseline and specific mutations,

8
00:00:15.209 --> 00:00:17.318
such as reversing a sign or doubling a

9
00:00:17.396 --> 00:00:18.063
coefficient.

10
00:00:18.431 --> 00:00:20.753
The question is whether tests detect deliberate changes.

11
00:00:21.072 --> 00:00:23.559
Each result stays linked to its parameters, code,

12
00:00:23.704 --> 00:00:25.155
and artifacts for later review.

13
00:00:25.581 --> 00:00:27.932
This separates model correctness from test sensitivity.

14
00:00:28.358 --> 00:00:30.196
If the program and oracle share a formula

15
00:00:30.264 --> 00:00:32.576
and integrator, they can share an error.

16
00:00:32.808 --> 00:00:35.469
So the suite compares distinct implementations at multiple

17
00:00:35.508 --> 00:00:36.185
observations.

18
00:00:36.552 --> 00:00:38.846
The contract defines success before results are known.

19
00:00:39.165 --> 00:00:41.564
A failing baseline blocks interpretation of its mutants;

20
00:00:41.883 --> 00:00:44.022
a small variation may survive if it falls

21
00:00:44.118 --> 00:00:44.960
below tolerance.

22
00:00:45.386 --> 00:00:46.962
The threshold is not changed afterward.

23
00:00:47.466 --> 00:00:49.865
The package preserves hashes and outputs so reviewers

24
00:00:49.913 --> 00:00:51.288
can trace each classification.

25
00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:55.332
We distinguish synthetic calculations, kernel controls, and earlier

26
00:00:55.389 --> 00:00:55.999
campaigns.

27
00:00:56.579 --> 00:00:59.888
I’m Cristian Guerra, known as criguex, a Colombian

28
00:00:59.947 --> 00:01:02.520
QA Automation professional from Medellín, with more than

29
00:01:02.617 --> 00:01:03.758
eight years of experience.

30
00:01:04.262 --> 00:01:07.077
I authored this QA study and independent reproduction

31
00:01:07.116 --> 00:01:11.489
through contributions to strategy, mutations, resources, and validation.

32
00:01:12.166 --> 00:01:14.449
AI tools are disclosed as assistance for analysis

33
00:01:14.508 --> 00:01:17.526
and code preparation, not as coauthors or co-discoverers.

34
00:01:18.029 --> 00:01:20.197
OpenAI is credited for the original proofs;

35
00:01:20.699 --> 00:01:22.392
this study does not claim authorship of them

36
00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:23.786
or discovery of a theorem.

37
00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:27.114
The contribution is making tests, detected failures, and

38
00:01:27.172 --> 00:01:28.082
limits auditable.

39
00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.180
The suite contains nine synthetic models:

40
00:01:30.383 --> 00:01:34.969
an RC circuit, Newton cooling, second-order consumption, Beer–Lambert

41
00:01:35.018 --> 00:01:38.732
attenuation, Snell refraction, a thin lens, an acoustic

42
00:01:38.781 --> 00:01:42.109
interface, an illustrative Fechner scale, and a synthetic

43
00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:43.203
logistic response.

44
00:01:43.783 --> 00:01:46.143
One concrete example is the RC circuit.

45
00:01:46.414 --> 00:01:49.220
With one kiloohm and one millifarad, its nominal

46
00:01:49.259 --> 00:01:51.001
time constant is one second.

47
00:01:51.503 --> 00:01:54.290
Deliberately changing tau changes the recorded output.

48
00:01:54.658 --> 00:01:58.198
These are reproducible calculations, not laboratory measurements.

49
00:01:58.566 --> 00:02:01.498
Each model has three nondegenerate configurations in the

50
00:02:01.546 --> 00:02:04.323
fixed contract, with units and observations specified.

51
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.312
The RC case runs for three seconds, with

52
00:02:07.361 --> 00:02:10.931
sixty-four, one hundred twenty-eight, and two hundred fifty-six

53
00:02:10.998 --> 00:02:11.918
integration steps.

54
00:02:12.237 --> 00:02:14.413
At three seconds and the finest resolution, the

55
00:02:14.472 --> 00:02:16.852
baseline records 4.751 volts;

56
00:02:17.122 --> 00:02:20.470
doubling tau records 3.884.

57
00:02:20.741 --> 00:02:23.218
These are rounded JSON values, not physical readings.

58
00:02:23.528 --> 00:02:26.033
The nominal time constant is resistance multiplied by

59
00:02:26.101 --> 00:02:26.884
capacitance:

60
00:02:27.088 --> 00:02:29.419
tau equals R times C.

61
00:02:29.845 --> 00:02:31.287
Other oracles are distinct:

62
00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:35.234
closed-form solutions for several ODEs, bisection for Snell,

63
00:02:35.553 --> 00:02:37.894
ray tracing for the lens, a boundary system

64
00:02:37.952 --> 00:02:41.193
for acoustics, and numerical integration for Fechner.

65
00:02:41.697 --> 00:02:43.806
The logistic model is a synthetic response to

66
00:02:43.873 --> 00:02:46.108
normalized stimulus, between zero and one;

67
00:02:46.688 --> 00:02:49.794
Fechner is illustrative, not a universal law.

68
00:02:50.065 --> 00:02:53.897
Some configurations share mathematical structure after rescaling, so

69
00:02:53.964 --> 00:02:56.944
nine names do not mean nine independent regimes.

70
00:02:57.525 --> 00:02:59.702
No experimental measurements were used.

71
00:03:00.205 --> 00:03:02.411
Plots retain units and calculated points.

72
00:03:02.913 --> 00:03:05.362
The suite examines detection of known changes in

73
00:03:05.429 --> 00:03:06.590
controlled examples;

74
00:03:07.016 --> 00:03:09.570
it does not certify real-world performance.

75
00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:11.535
The kernel control uses a minimal fixture:

76
00:03:11.738 --> 00:03:14.215
target states zero equals zero and is proved

77
00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:14.998
with rfl.

78
00:03:15.318 --> 00:03:17.427
The mutation keeps the declared type but replaces

79
00:03:17.456 --> 00:03:19.188
the proof value with a proof of True.

80
00:03:19.613 --> 00:03:21.568
Lean and nanoda accept the baseline and reject

81
00:03:21.597 --> 00:03:22.652
that incompatible value.

82
00:03:22.971 --> 00:03:25.167
This is a typechecking control for one declaration,

83
00:03:25.312 --> 00:03:27.402
contrasting the declared type with the exported proof

84
00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:27.838
value.

85
00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:30.759
Separately, Lean accepts a nonzero constant field in

86
00:03:30.818 --> 00:03:33.497
periodic Navier–Stokes, with zero pressure and force and

87
00:03:33.574 --> 00:03:34.426
unit viscosity.

88
00:03:35.007 --> 00:03:36.777
These controls have distinct scopes.

89
00:03:36.922 --> 00:03:38.441
Lean reports that True does not match the

90
00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:39.253
expected type;

91
00:03:39.622 --> 00:03:41.885
nanoda reaches a definitional-equality assertion.

92
00:03:42.204 --> 00:03:43.811
This pair is a bounded control.

93
00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:45.881
The periodic example is on a torus, and

94
00:03:45.939 --> 00:03:47.719
its axiom report lists three axioms:

95
00:03:48.145 --> 00:03:50.728
propext, Classical.choice, and Quot.sound.

96
00:03:51.308 --> 00:03:53.224
A constant velocity does not have finite energy

97
00:03:53.272 --> 00:03:54.975
over all of R³, so it does not

98
00:03:54.995 --> 00:03:56.408
transfer to the Euclidean problem.

99
00:03:56.988 --> 00:03:59.736
After the clean-source build, Comparator independently rechecked the

100
00:03:59.784 --> 00:04:02.609
Navier–Stokes and Euler challenges with both nanoda and

101
00:04:02.677 --> 00:04:03.035
Lean.

102
00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:06.179
Calibration included two positive fixtures accepted and four

103
00:04:06.228 --> 00:04:08.491
negative fixtures rejected before kernel calls.

104
00:04:08.994 --> 00:04:11.568
These recorded results are not universal verification.

105
00:04:11.935 --> 00:04:14.596
Exact names appear on screen, and preserved artifacts

106
00:04:14.663 --> 00:04:17.605
let reviewers inspect the harness, declarations, and outputs

107
00:04:17.643 --> 00:04:19.647
without changing original theorem sources.

108
00:04:19.667 --> 00:04:22.154
The suite ran on macOS arm64 and Linux

109
00:04:22.357 --> 00:04:23.730
x86_64.

110
00:04:24.234 --> 00:04:26.798
Each environment evaluated the same eighty-four variants:

111
00:04:26.972 --> 00:04:30.494
twenty-seven baseline PASS, fifty-four mutant KILLED, and three

112
00:04:30.532 --> 00:04:32.041
tiny calibration SURVIVED.

113
00:04:32.467 --> 00:04:34.973
Classifications and parameters match across hosts.

114
00:04:35.244 --> 00:04:36.975
These are paired runs of one suite, not

115
00:04:37.034 --> 00:04:38.959
one hundred sixty-eight distinct cases.

116
00:04:39.385 --> 00:04:41.880
Survivors remain in the report without forcing rejection.

117
00:04:42.384 --> 00:04:44.755
Counts are per host, with explicit denominators;

118
00:04:45.074 --> 00:04:46.738
another platform added no cases.

119
00:04:47.241 --> 00:04:49.650
This distinction matters when reporting totals and comparing

120
00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:51.779
results across both hosts side by side.

121
00:04:52.359 --> 00:04:55.039
The comparison included seven hundred thirty-eight finite values

122
00:04:55.271 --> 00:04:57.816
and eighteen non-finite outputs from the chemical sign-reversal

123
00:04:57.855 --> 00:04:59.645
mutant, represented as null.

124
00:05:00.573 --> 00:05:03.127
The largest normalized difference between finite values was

125
00:05:03.166 --> 00:05:06.059
about 1.11 times ten to the minus sixteen.

126
00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:09.349
Each baseline uses an independent oracle and normalized

127
00:05:09.406 --> 00:05:11.815
error tolerance of 10⁻⁶ against a fixed scale.

128
00:05:12.241 --> 00:05:14.234
ODEs use their last applicable resolution;

129
00:05:14.554 --> 00:05:17.069
algebraic models receive no invented refinements.

130
00:05:17.388 --> 00:05:20.329
In fifteen ODE baselines, error decreased with refinement

131
00:05:20.532 --> 00:05:22.206
and observed orders were near four;

132
00:05:22.525 --> 00:05:24.461
this is diagnostic, not a general bound.

133
00:05:24.606 --> 00:05:27.257
The largest fine ODE error was about 1.12

134
00:05:27.295 --> 00:05:29.182
times ten to the minus nine in a

135
00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:30.159
logistic case.

136
00:05:30.585 --> 00:05:33.294
Fechner reached about 7.63 times ten to the

137
00:05:33.343 --> 00:05:35.480
minus eight with a trapezoidal oracle.

138
00:05:35.906 --> 00:05:38.277
Tiny RC mutations survive under this contract;

139
00:05:38.548 --> 00:05:39.979
that does not establish equivalence.

140
00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:42.873
The campaign tests detection of known changes and

141
00:05:42.921 --> 00:05:44.324
cross-platform consistency.

142
00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:47.362
JSON and classifications were preserved when CSV export

143
00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:48.175
was corrected.

144
00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.880
The review package links code, records, and reproducible

145
00:05:50.909 --> 00:05:51.287
checks.

146
00:05:51.606 --> 00:05:53.618
Public release follows author approval.

147
00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:56.318
Reproducing files is not repeating experiments.

148
00:05:56.637 --> 00:05:58.649
The useful result is a traceable path from

149
00:05:58.717 --> 00:05:59.646
contract to data.

150
00:06:00.013 --> 00:06:03.071
This helps audit decisions, catch export mistakes, and

151
00:06:03.119 --> 00:06:05.306
preserve criteria fixed before execution.

152
00:06:05.886 --> 00:06:08.643
Earlier campaigns are documented separately, with parameters and

153
00:06:08.682 --> 00:06:09.911
results preserved for review.

154
00:06:10.337 --> 00:06:13.898
Local verification confirmed artifact integrity, CSV rows, and

155
00:06:13.965 --> 00:06:15.233
cross-host correspondence.

156
00:06:15.658 --> 00:06:17.758
Clean03 completed the source build with exit code

157
00:06:17.932 --> 00:06:20.689
zero and 11,424 jobs;

158
00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:23.224
it reused dependencies and toolchain cache, so it

159
00:06:23.252 --> 00:06:24.259
was not a full bootstrap.

160
00:06:24.762 --> 00:06:27.364
After that build, Comparator rechecked the Navier–Stokes and

161
00:06:27.423 --> 00:06:29.493
Euler challenges with both nanoda and Lean.

162
00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:32.453
Earlier ODE context is separate from this suite:

163
00:06:32.773 --> 00:06:34.379
one hundred fifty recorded runs in groups of

164
00:06:34.457 --> 00:06:37.600
ninety, thirty, and thirty, not one hundred fifty

165
00:06:37.648 --> 00:06:38.674
independent cases.

166
00:06:39.042 --> 00:06:41.180
Maximum errors were about 1.30 times ten to

167
00:06:41.219 --> 00:06:43.134
the minus five at step 0.05;

168
00:06:43.512 --> 00:06:45.862
7.24 times ten to the minus seven at

169
00:06:45.911 --> 00:06:47.043
0.025;

170
00:06:47.275 --> 00:06:49.346
and 4.27 times ten to the minus eight

171
00:06:49.578 --> 00:06:53.245
at 0.0125, against fine tolerance 10⁻⁶.

172
00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:55.218
Taylor–Green V1 illustrates flow;

173
00:06:55.461 --> 00:06:56.951
it is not a formal construction or evidence

174
00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:57.502
of blow-up.

175
00:06:57.772 --> 00:07:00.201
The contribution is contracts, failures detected by known

176
00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:03.336
mutations, repetition across two environments, and traceable evidence.

177
00:07:04.129 --> 00:07:07.873
Cristian Guerra, criguex, QA Automation, receives credit for

178
00:07:07.893 --> 00:07:09.760
the QA study and independent reproduction;

179
00:07:10.079 --> 00:07:12.005
AI is listed as assistance.

180
00:07:12.431 --> 00:07:14.366
OpenAI is credited for the original proofs.

181
00:07:14.733 --> 00:07:16.358
No new theorem or validation of an open

182
00:07:16.417 --> 00:07:17.994
